  "reason": "Evidence: config_022 (transformer aggregation, scvi_n200, resnet50, concat) achieved 0.688 acc, clearly outperforming config_011 (avgpool, same other settings) at 0.632 acc, establishing transformer aggregation as the strong baseline. The largest untested lever is the image encoder: resnet50 may be a bottleneck relative to the much larger imagenet_vit_l. Question: Does upgrading the image encoder to ViT-L (pretrained on ImageNet) while keeping the proven transformer+concat+scvi_n200+multiprofile pipeline yield a meaningful accuracy gain? This is a clean single-variable change from our best result. Rationale: With 7 experiments remaining, testing the highest-impact architectural upgrade (image encoder capacity) is the best use of the next slot; if ViT-L helps, it opens a new high-performing branch to exploit. Expected relative cost: moderate-to-high (~7-9 GPU hours) due to the larger ViT-L backbone, but justified by the potential accuracy ceiling it unlocks."
